==Hunting technique==
The hunting technique is the same as for other [[Hunter#Pitfall trapping|pitfall trapping]]. Players must bring a [[teasing stick]], a [[knife]], and any type of [[Woodcutting#Types_of_trees|logs]] (except for [[redwood logs]] or [[Arctic pine logs|artic pine logs]]) to the hunting spot location. By clicking on a pit, the player will create a [[Pitfall|spiked pit]]. After this, the player should tease a sabre-toothed kyatt, lure it towards the set up trap, and jump over the trap. If successful, the creature will attempt to walk over the trap, and fall into the pit. If unsuccessful, the creature will jump over the trap and be unable to be caught by the same trap requiring the player to create a second trap in order to catch it. Finally, the player needs to dismantle the trap in order to get rewarded with the loot and Hunter experience. Using a [[hunter's spear]] instead of a teasing stick will decrease the chance of the trap being jumped over by 5%, which doesn't consume the spear.

It is advised to bring an [[axe]] to the hunter area, since the player could cut [[dead tree]]s for an unlimited supply of logs while hunting these creatures, and a [[bonecrusher]] to automatically bury the [[big bones]]. After obtaining 25 Hunters' rumours and reaching level 51 [[Cooking]], the player may bring a [[tinderbox]] to cook and eat the [[Sabre-toothed kyatt]], restoring 17 [[Hitpoints]].  Players can also catch the [[Snowy knight|Snowy Knight]] butterflies in the area to restore their hitpoints.

